      "writtenOn": "2022-01-18T01:32:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Are you sure this is correct?\n\nWe\u0027ve often seen hard-to-debug leaks when extracting FDs from ParcelFileDescriptors. IIRC, the issue is that ParcelFileDescriptor has a finalize method that will close the wrapped fd. The finalizer runs at at some unpredictable time after the ParcelFileDescriptor goes out of scope. This can result in the socket being closed while it\u0027s still being used.\n\nIn some places we\u0027ve worked around it by doing things like:\n\n    FileDescriptor fd \u003d new FileDescriptor();\n    fd.setInt$(pfd.detachFd());\n\nbut I don\u0027t know if that is correct here. In particular, if you do that, it doesn\u0027t seem possible for the caller to close the fd any more, resulting in a filedescriptor leak. Another solution is to keep the fd in scope so the finalizer does not run, but that doesn\u0027t seem to be possible in a utility method such as this one.\n\nA better solution might be to always keep the pfd itself in scope. Not sure if that\u0027s something you can do here.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 93,
        "startChar": 28,
        "endLine": 93,
        "endChar": 51
      },
      "revId": "2534244b374a47e99c59197510fb685ce2a91e53",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "872c6324_e646506b",
        "filename": "core/java/android/net/LocalSocket.java",
        "patchSetId": 5
