      "writtenOn": "2022-01-18T20:30:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Good to know ! I only put the Parcel because I wasn\u0027t allowed by compiler to build an API with FileDescriptor as a parameter.\n\nWe are currently calling this API by doing something like this:\n```\n LocalSocket.createConnectedLocalSocket(mPfd.getFileDescriptor());\n```\nand the mPfd is keep in scope of the BluetoothSocket and close on it\u0027s own.\n\nSo moving the `getFileDescriptor` from being before the API call to after shouldn\u0027t change the behavior if I understand correctly what you said.\n\n(cf https://source.corp.google.com/android/packages/modules/Bluetooth/framework/java/android/bluetooth/BluetoothSocket.java?q\u003dcreateConnectedLocalSocket%20mPfd\u0026sq\u003dp:%5Eandroid$)\n\nI put this comment as resolved, but if I miss something here do note hesitate to re-open and we will see how we can keep the ParcelFileDescriptor in the LocalSocketImpl scope by adding a constructor.",
      "parentUuid": "654dc6c7_3ab6362f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 93,
        "startChar": 28,
        "endLine": 93,
        "endChar": 51
      },
      "revId": "2534244b374a47e99c59197510fb685ce2a91e53",
